<title>INDIA: India M3 money supply falls to 15.9 pct on Feb 28.</title>
<headline>India M3 money supply falls to 15.9 pct on Feb 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth was 15.9 percent on February 28, 1997, down from 16.1 percent on February 14, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Feb 28, 1997   Feb 14, 1997  Mar 1, 1996</p>
<p>		   15.9	     16.1	    15.22</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,783.77 billion rupees on February 28, 1997 against 6,750.33 billion on February 14, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
